The '''Wolfpack''' was a [[Clone trooper/Legends|clone trooper]] [[Squad/Legends|squad]] in the [[Grand Army of the Republic/Legends|Grand Army of the Republic's]] [[104th Battalion/Legends|104th Battalion]] that served under [[Jedi General/Legends|Jedi General]] [[Plo Koon/Legends|Plo Koon]] and [[Clone Commander/Legends|Clone Commander]] [[Wolffe/Legends|Wolffe]] during the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]].

==Description==
Members of the Wolfpack became reputed for being experts at difficult extractions under fire.<ref name="TCWEG">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Episode Guide]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:Phase_1_Clone_Trooper_of_the_104th_Battalion.png|thumb|left|250px|A Wolfpack clone trooper in their original Phase I colors]]
The Wolfpack's members included Marshal [[Clone Commander/Legends|Commander]] [[Wolffe/Legends|Wolffe]], [[Clone Sergeant/Legends|Sergeant]] [[Sinker/Legends|Sinker]] and [[Boost/Legends|Boost]]. Following the [[Battle of Abregado/Legends|attack]] on the [[Venator-class Star Destroyer/Legends|''Venator''-class Star Destroyer]] [[Triumphant/Legends|''Triumphant'']] by the [[Malevolence/Legends|''Malevolence'']] in the [[Abregado system/Legends|Abregado system]], Plo Koon, Wolffe, Sinker, and Boost were trapped in an [[Escape pod/Legends|escape pod]] and fought off [[Battle droid/Legends|battle droids]] searching the wreckage for surviving [[Cloning/Legends|clones]]. They were saved by [[General/Legends|General]] [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Jedi Commander/Legends|Commander]] [[Ahsoka Tano/Legends|Ahsoka Tano]].<ref name="TCWRM">{{TCW|Rising Malevolence}}</ref>

Due to the loss of so many members at the Battle of Abregado, Wolffe and the other members of the Wolfpack changed the color of their armor from a rusty red to a dark grey blue, to honor their fallen brothers with a melancholy color. The Wolfpack also changed their symbol to more match the markings on Wolffe's helmet.

Soon after the Battle of Abregado, the surviving members of the Wolfpack donned Cold Assault Gear and participated in the [[Battle of Khorm/Legends|Battle of Khorm]]. After the battle, Wolffe received reinforcements to replenish the Wolfpack's numbers.

After the addition of new recruits, the Wolfpack helped Koon and Tano [[Mission to Vanqor/Legends|rescue]] Generals Skywalker and [[Mace Windu/Legends|Mace Windu]] from the collapsing [[Bridge (starship)/Legends|bridge]] of the [[Star Destroyer/Legends|Star Destroyer]] [[Endurance/Legends|''Endurance'']] on [[Vanqor/Legends|Vanqor]] following [[Boba Fett/Legends|Boba Fett's]] [[Sabotage of the Endurance/Legends|sabotage]] of the [[Cruiser/Legends|cruiser]].

[[File:Wolfpack_Felucia.png|thumb|right|300px|The Wolfpack with Plo Koon on Felucia.]]
Later, two members of the Wolfpack, Wolffe and Comet, helped in the rescue mission to [[Lola Sayu/Legends|Lola Sayu]], to retrieve Koon, Anakin Skywalker, Tano, and the other survivors of the raid on the [[Citadel/Legends|Citadel]]. They later participated in the [[Second Battle of Felucia/Legends|Second Battle of Felucia]] with Koon, Skywalker and Tano.

Later in the war, the Wolfpack was sent on a relief effort to the planet [[Aleen/Legends|Aleen]] where catastrophic [[Groundquake/Legends|groundquakes]] had inflicted mass casualties among the natives. Soon after, they participated in the [[Rescue of Adi Gallia/Legends|rescue]] of [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Adi Gallia/Legends|Adi Gallia]] from the hands of [[General/Legends|General]] [[Grievous/Legends|Grievous]].

They later were [[Battle of Kadavo/Legends|sent]] to [[Kadavo/Legends|Kadavo]] to rescue [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi/Legends|Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Anakin Skywalker/Legends|Anakin Skywalker]], [[Ahsoka Tano/Legends|Ahsoka Tano]] and the [[Battle of Kiros|kidnapped]] [[Togruta/Legends|Togrutan]] slaves.

